{"seq":12,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T22:36:49.492Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"e3d9ed871ce0da089b9399043ebda498cb2c40bd9ed9f706c939f9e360d1f305","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina, I found four items across the Coastal channels and Moss's notes. Only the Coastal cheat sheet and your Pellucid cutover recap named tickets or feature requests for these two accounts. #coastal-team and #coastal-random had none.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (Gulf Coast)**\n- **Ticket #4419** is open. The `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. Source: Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.\n- **Ticket #PD-8841** covers how Pemberline Dock handles chassis pool holds on double-booked gates (Gate 4B). Source: your 2025-12-08 cutover recap. I can't tell whether it's still open.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (Puget Sound)**\n- **Feature request #882** is a bulk-clear button for departed barges, asked for by their warehouse managers. Source: Moss's cheat sheet.\n- The cheat sheet also mentions a failed tide-table import macro on Terminal B. Engineering gave the night dispatcher a manual CSV patch. There's no ticket number, so I've left it out of the list.\n\n**Left out on purpose**\n- Ticket #8812, the Door 4B scanner issue, belongs to Sofia's retail account (Covey & Lark, now Pellow Home Living), not Pellucid.\n- PD-4827 and the other Saltmarsh items belong to a different account.\n\nMoss's Coastal notes are the only notes I could reach, and I couldn't list any files in Moss's own notes folder. A fuller ticket system may have more for these accounts, so check it before Kwame's review."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
